---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Practical AI Solutions for Business Workflows | Emon Hossain"
  description="Explore evidence-first AI customer operations, workflow automation and owner-controlled websites with human safeguards and measurable pilots."
>
  <header class="container hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">PRACTICAL AI · OPERATIONS · HUMAN CONTROL</div>
    <h1>Start with the <span class="gradient-text">work that needs to change.</span></h1>
    <p>AI is useful when it helps a business finish a specific job more reliably. These notes describe common problems, possible workflows and necessary controls without claiming unverified client results, prices or guaranteed outcomes.</p>
    <p lang="bn" style="font-family:'Noto Sans Bengali',system-ui,sans-serif;color:var(--brand-stone-600);max-width:45rem;line-height:1.9;margin-top:1rem;">কোন কাজ বারবার আটকে যায়? সেই সমস্যা থেকে শুরু করে AI ও automation-এর বাস্তব প্রয়োগ বোঝার জন্য এই গাইডগুলো তৈরি।</p>
    <div class="hero-cta"><a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Discuss a workflow</a><a href="/services" class="btn-outline">Ways to work together</a></div>
  </header>
  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="paths">
    <div class="section-title"><div class="eyebrow">THREE PRACTICAL STARTING POINTS</div><h2 id="paths">Choose a problem, not a buzzword.</h2><p>Each guide separates example design from verified outcomes and identifies what needs checking.</p></div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <a class="entity-card" href="/solutions/customer-operations"><div class="role">MESSAGES → ACTION</div><h3>AI Customer Support & Sales Operations</h3><p>Enquiry capture, Bangla/Banglish replies, lead ownership, staff review and CRM handoffs.</p><div class="arrow">Explore customer operations →</div></a>
      <a class="entity-card" href="/solutions/workflow-automation"><div class="role">REPETITION → RELIABILITY</div><h3>Business Workflow Automation</h3><p>Approvals, documents, APIs and data routing with errors, logs and human control.</p><div class="arrow">Explore workflow automation →</div></a>
      <a class="entity-card" href="/solutions/websites-lead-operations"><div class="role">VISITOR → QUALIFIED ENQUIRY</div><h3>Owner-Controlled Websites & Leads</h3><p>Useful pages, search foundations, verified contact routes and measurable follow-up.</p><div class="arrow">Explore website operations →</div></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section data-section" aria-labelledby="approach">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-title"><div class="eyebrow">PROOF OVER HYPE</div><h2 id="approach" style="color:white;">A practical approach to AI adoption</h2><p style="color:var(--brand-steel);">A useful implementation has a baseline, an owner and a way to recover safely.</p></div>
      <div class="data-grid">
        <div class="data-item"><div class="num">Understand the current process</div><div class="label">Map triggers, exceptions, systems, permissions and intended outcomes.</div></div>
        <div class="data-item"><div class="num">Test a bounded workflow</div><div class="label">Prefer simple rules; use AI only where language or interpretation helps.</div></div>
        <div class="data-item"><div class="num">Measure and hand off</div><div class="label">Compare against baseline; document errors, costs, ownership and rollback.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="scope">
    <div class="section-title"><div class="eyebrow">ACCOUNTABILITY</div><h2 id="scope">Not every task needs AI.</h2><p>Sometimes a clearer process, a rules-based integration or a simpler website is the right solution. Commercial delivery is considered through the appropriate SYSmoAI business context, with agreed terms for each engagement.</p></div>
    <div class="hero-cta" style="justify-content:center;"><a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Share the process you want to improve</a><a href="/about" class="btn-outline">About Emon</a></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
